dialogue cohesion_cleric_knight
title: Behind the shield
trigger: Cohesion cleric knight level=2
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker cleric cleric
speaker knight knight

node open commander
  The Knight sits with the shield arm held out stiff while the Cleric works a strap of linen round it. The bruise runs from wrist to elbow, and neither of them is pretending it doesn't.
  -> stayed

node stayed cleric
  You stayed in front of me for three hits that weren't yours. I called you back twice. You heard me.
  -> before

node before knight
  I heard. Stand before the hold. It doesn't say step aside when the healer asks. If I'd moved, they'd have been on you.
  -> spare

node spare cleric
  And if you'd dropped, they'd have been on both of us, and I'd have had nobody to wrap. Commander, settle this. Who stands where?
  * The Cleric calls the Knight back, and the Knight goes. That's an order. -> order
    do: AddCohesion cleric knight 10
    do: AddTrust knight -3
    do: SetFlag cleric_knight:line_order
  * The Knight stands in front. The Cleric keeps the Knight standing. -> front
    do: AddCohesion cleric knight 6
    do: SetFlag cleric_knight:line_front
  * Keep the Cleric out of the line. The Knight holds it alone. -> alone
    do: AddCohesion cleric knight -4
    do: AddTrust knight 2
    do: SetFlag cleric_knight:line_alone
  * The oath was to the hold's people. The Cleric is one of them now. Stand before, and listen. -> people
    if: FlagSet knight:oath_people
    do: AddCohesion cleric knight 8
    do: SetFlag cleric_knight:line_people

node order knight
  Back when called. I'll go. I'll hate it, and I'll go. Call early, Cleric. I'm slow to turn with this much shield.
  -> levy

node front cleric
  Keep you standing. That's a job I know. I'll stand closer, then, so I don't have to shout.
  -> levy

node alone knight
  Alone, then. I've held a line alone before. Never liked it. Mind your distance, Cleric.
  -> levy

node people knight
  One of the hold's. I never thought of it like that. Before you, and listening. I can try both at once.
  -> levy

node levy knight
  You wore the white. The levy came through the holds with collectors behind it. My sister carries water at the well there. If they took her to a table, would you know her colour on sight?
  * We go to the sister first, before anything. The Cleric comes, to see her colour before anyone else does. -> first
    if: FlagSet knight:sister_promised
    do: AddCohesion cleric knight 10
    do: AddTrust knight 2
    do: SetFlag cleric_knight:sister_first
  * Write the sister in the book of names, on the living page. -> living
    do: AddCohesion cleric knight 8
    do: SetFlag cleric_knight:sister_living
  * Read the Knight one name from the book, the way you read me one. -> read
    if: FlagSet cleric:thread_read
    do: AddCohesion cleric knight 8
    do: AddTrust cleric 2
    do: SetFlag cleric_knight:sister_read
  * She isn't lost. She doesn't belong in that book. -> not
    do: AddCohesion cleric knight 2
    do: SetFlag cleric_knight:sister_not

node first cleric
  First. I'll know. A water carrier has strong hands and a straight back, and the colour sits in the cheeks. If it's still there, I'll tell you before you've finished asking.
  -> close

node living cleric
  The living page has three names on it. She'll be the fourth. Tell me how she spells it. Slowly.
  -> close

node read cleric
  One name. A boy from the river holds who drew horses on the table with his finger. I never knew if it was a good sign. I'd like it to be.
  -> close

node not knight
  No. She isn't. Leave the book shut. If she ever goes in it, it'll be because we were too slow, and we won't be.
  -> close

node close commander
  The Cleric ties off the linen. The Knight flexes the arm, picks up the shield, and sets it down again on the Cleric's side of the fire.
